WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.160
As flame rises, so does it fade

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:05.160
such is the way of things.

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:10.380
Light and dark, neither can fade, while the other survives.

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:13.240
This is the lore of the dark souls universe

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:17.280
and all the characters within are bound by its principles.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.700
But it was not always this way.

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:27.180
Once, long ago, the world was grey, without heat, cold, life, death, light or dark.

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:29.740
But then, the first flame appeared,

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:32.340
after the advent of fire

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:36.420
the ancient lords found the three souls,

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:41.880
but your progenitor found a fourth unique soul,

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:44.160
the Dark Soul.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:48.320
Your ancestor claimed the dark soul

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:51.520
and waited for fire to subside.

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:57.700
And soon, the flames did fade, and only dark remained.

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:03.720
Thus began the age of men, the age of dark.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:09.780
This was the natural progression that was supposed to take place in the world, it was supposed to be

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:13.950
the age of ancients and then the age of fire, then the dark age of man.

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:28.760
However, Lord Gwyn trembled at the
dark clinging to his age of fire and in dire
fear of humans and the Dark Lord who would one day be born amongst them.

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:40.100
Lord Gwyn resisted the course of nature by sacrificing himself to link the fire and commanding his children to shepherd the humans.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:47.320
Gwyn has blurred your past the prevent the birth of the Dark Lord

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:53.300
What Gwyn did could be called the First Sin. For he resisted the course
of nature.

00:01:53.420 --> 00:02:00.780
He forced the darkness back and from
this moment forth, the light and the dark have been in a constant ebb and flow

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:03.900
Like the rising and the falling of the
tide.

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:07.600
In the ending of Dark Souls 1, we are a
part of this flow.

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:12.120
The world is in the grip of darkness,
filled with broken tired characters.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:18.020
We tear through the remains of their fragile world and are guided to the kiln of the first flame.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:25.260
Here we have a choice, we can do the same thing Gwyn did and bolster the power of the flame with our own soul.

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:30.380
Or we can turn our back on the dying
light and let darkness grip the world.

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:35.200
Before Dark Souls 2, we thought that
these endings were polar opposites.

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:36.600
But we were wrong.

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:42.700
The choice itself is irrelevant and whether you link to the flame or whether you turned your back on it.

00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:46.320
Your choice would have led to the events
of Dark Souls 2.

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:51.049
It would have led to the kingdom of
Drangleic, where our character exists.

00:02:51.049 --> 00:02:59.900
Drangleic was once a proud kingdom of
light but it has fallen into darkness and
decay like the countless kingdoms before it

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:04.640
No flame, however brilliant, does not one day splutter and

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:07.760
fade but then

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:11.580
from the ashes, the flame reignites

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:17.640
and a new kingdom is born, sporting a
new face.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:20.040
It is all a curse.

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:20.820
"Laughs"

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:26.020
And it is your cursed flesh that will inherit the flame.

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:27.260
"More laughing"

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:35.520
In the ending of Dark Souls 2, we once again arrive at the kiln to either link the fire or let the world fade into darkness.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:43.420
Once the fire is linked souls will flourish anew and all of this will play out again.

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:48.240
It is your choice to embrace or renounce
this.

00:03:48.680 --> 00:04:00.760
The Emerald Herald pushes us to link the
fire for she wishes to be free of the curse.
It reminds me of Anastacia from Dark Souls 1, a fire keeper who also wished for us to link the fire.

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:06.340
Frampt has told me of you , that you have agreed to link to the fire.

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:08.840
I thank you sincerely.

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:15.080
Finally the curse of the Undead will be lifted and I can die human.

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:30.640
To link the fire is to become free of the curse of the undead and if linking the fire frees us of the curse, then it does follow that the initial linking of the fire, the thing that started all of this is related to the curse.

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:33.700
Aldia says as much after
all.

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:42.040
Once, the Lord of Light banished Dark, and all that stemmed from humanity.

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:46.940
And men assumed a fleeting form.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:52.840
These are the roots of our world.

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:54.960
What Aldia is saying

00:04:54.960 --> 00:05:00.080
is that when Gwyn linked to the fire and
banished Dark, man became much less.

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:02.980
He says that man assumed a fleeting form.

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:13.080
Fleeting means temporary, so I take this
to mean that Gwyn reduced mankind's existence in some way but what exactly? Did he make them mortal?

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:16.080
Did he place the undead curse upon them?

00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:19.000
Causing them to return to their hollow state?

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:26.360
And as far as I know there's nothing in the game that explicitly explains what Gwyn's linking of the flame did to man.

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:30.380
My current theory is that Gwen actually linked the fire to humanity.

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:32.440
Which would explain a lot.

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:39.200
By doing this, he could feed the flame with humanity's souls plus it would explain why we respawn at the bonfire.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:46.700
Why we kindle the bonfire and why we're
drawn to it even though our nature is inherently dark.

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:51.660
Agdayne says : "In the past, humans were one with the dark"

00:05:52.440 --> 00:06:06.980
and we are one with it no longer. : "Men are props on the stage of life, and no matter how tender, how exquisite... A lie will remain a lie!"

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:09.360
Men became something to be used.

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:16.980
You can hear the fury in his voice when he says this because Aldia realizes that men were supposed to inherit the world

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:23.280
but they can't because the world seems
stuck in a cycle of Light and Dark.

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:27.029
Men had everything taken from them but
this defines them.

00:06:27.029 --> 00:06:30.199
They are fateless but they still want
for more.

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:37.700
And so they loved, they lost and they
achieved all within the bounds of their desire.

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:41.200
Peace grants men the illusion of life.

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:47.229
While the flame is at its height and the world is peaceful, mankind seems able to die.

00:06:47.229 --> 00:06:55.060
We know this because the curse of undeath is always listed as something that appears rather than something that has
always existed.

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:59.200
Usually this happens sometime after the
fire has been linked.

00:06:59.209 --> 00:07:02.699
Perhaps as soon as it begins to fade, for
example,

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:05.820
Gwyn was undead long after he links the
fire.

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:10.819
And similarly Vendrick started to fear the curse after his reign had begun.

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:16.960
He began to fear men who would not die,
Men who were cursed to return to their hollow state.

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:23.080
Shackled by falsehoods, they yearn for love, unaware of its grand illusion.

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:29.160
Until the curse touches their flesh.

00:07:30.460 --> 00:07:32.760
We are bound by this yoke.

00:07:33.900 --> 00:07:38.280
As true as the Dark that churns within men.

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:41.560
This is the fate that the Emerald Herald,

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:45.760
Vendrick and Anastacia want to avoid by linking the fire.

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:51.580
They want to be free from the curse of the undead so that they can become human and die.

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:55.700
Better to die than to become a soulless husk like you see in the trailer.

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:58.900
So in the original ending of Dark
Souls 2,

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:02.770
you could choose to link the fire or you
can choose to let it fade

00:08:02.770 --> 00:08:05.810
both are irrelevant because the world of

00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:11.080
Dark Souls 2 is defined by the countless
civilizations that have risen and fallen.

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:13.880
This one ending where you ascend the throne

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:17.930
and the Emerald Herald tells you, you
can link the fire a walk away from it

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:21.470
is the same as the two endings of Dark
Souls 1,

00:08:21.470 --> 00:08:27.780
because whether you link the fire or
extend the age of Dark, you become part of the cycle.

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:31.980
So Dark Souls 2 gives you no in-game
choice to be made

00:08:31.980 --> 00:08:38.100
because in this game you are supposed
to have learned today is no significant choice to be made.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:42.120
If you link the fire, the cycle renews
and if you choose not to,

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:46.640
eventually an undead will rise who can
unseat you and link the fire.

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:50.180
That's who your character in Dark Souls 2 is after all.

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:52.680
Vendrick was the Lord of
Light before you

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:58.800
but after spending countless years researching the curse, he realized that it was all futile.

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:03.100
His soul's description says that he is the one who should have linked the fire

00:09:03.220 --> 00:09:08.740
but he became overwhelmed by despair and seems to have accepted the darkness instead.

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:13.300
One day fire will fade and Dark will
become a curse

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:18.560
Men will be free from death left to wander eternally.

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:24.800
Dark will again be ours and in our crude shape, we can bury the false legends of yore.

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:28.580
Vendrick is inclined to believe that
there are two choices:

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:30.680
To link the fire or let it fade.

00:09:30.940 --> 00:09:38.360
He believes that by accepting the darkness the world will eventually pass into an age
of man built around their dark souls.

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:42.340
Only is this our only choice?

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:44.540
And while it is true,

00:09:44.540 --> 00:09:48.930
that we have never seen exactly what
happens once the flame fades entirely.

00:09:48.930 --> 00:09:52.329
Aldia is a character who believes that
it never will.

00:09:52.329 --> 00:09:56.300
Young Hollow, there are but two paths.

00:09:56.309 --> 00:10:02.000
Inherit the order of this world, or destroy it.

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:09.500
But only a true monarch can make such a choice.

00:10:10.660 --> 00:10:12.560
To link the fire or to let it fade.

00:10:12.780 --> 00:10:15.339
These aren't two choices, they are one.

00:10:15.339 --> 00:10:18.499
This is what Aldia calls inheriting
the order

00:10:18.499 --> 00:10:21.720
of the world. It's the order Gwyn began
long ago

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:26.000
when he linked the flame, forcing the
darkness and the light into a constant ebb and flow.

00:10:26.699 --> 00:10:29.699
A cycle that would repeat itself
throughout the centuries

00:10:29.699 --> 00:10:34.849
but Aldia tells us a second choice, not
to inherit the order of the world,

00:10:34.849 --> 00:10:39.720
but, to destroy the cycle entirely and
this is exactly the ending.

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:46.700
Dark Souls 2 needed. For we are the one
undead in history who is able to ignore the hollowing effects of the curse.

00:10:46.840 --> 00:10:53.600
And in my previous video on this topic, I
told you about the effects of gathering the three crowns from the DLC.

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:55.899
When you have the three crowns

00:10:55.899 --> 00:10:59.939
it doesn't cure the undead curse, it stops
you from hollowing

00:10:59.940 --> 00:11:06.400
and once you have united the crowns
of Lords long past, you have the ability to ignore your fate.

00:11:06.880 --> 00:11:10.020
You can now exist outside of the cycle.

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:13.020
For while every other undead is immortal.

00:11:13.320 --> 00:11:19.660
You are the only one who will never be broken by the curse and you were the one who will never hollow.

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:22.580
Many monarchs have come and gone.

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:28.280
One drowned in poison, another succumbed to flame.

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:33.780
Still another slumbers in a realm of ice.

00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:40.500
Not one of them stood here, as you do now.

00:11:42.900 --> 00:11:47.000
You, conquerer of adversities.

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:51.500
Give us your answer.

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:57.570
Throughout the entire game, we've been told that we do without really knowing why.

00:11:57.570 --> 00:12:03.340
But that is exactly what it means to be man, it is exactly what is required of you in the end.

00:12:03.560 --> 00:12:08.720
For there is no path and we are
the one undead who can forge forward.

00:12:08.860 --> 00:12:12.260
Forging a new path and bringing us into a new age.

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:18.880
Not an age of ancients which passed naturally not an age of fire which Gwyn failed to implement.

00:12:19.020 --> 00:12:22.290
Nor an age of Dark which Nashandra
perished by.

00:12:22.290 --> 00:12:25.480
We are the true monarch, who cannot perish,

00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:29.220
who cannot hollow and we seek to break
free of the cycle.

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:32.350
To march forward bravely into an
uncertain future.

00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:53.800
There is no path.

00:13:01.220 --> 00:13:05.200
Beyond the scope of light, beyond the reach of Dark...

00:13:10.730 --> 00:13:13.500
What could possible await us?

00:13:24.629 --> 00:13:28.000
And yet, we seek it, insatiably...

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:32.000
Such is our fate.

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:43.000
Thanks for watching!

